The reason the array is treated differently when it comes from a function return vs when it's literally declared is because of the way strings are handled in PowerShell. When a function returns an array, each element in the array is a separate string, not a single string that includes the delimiter. When a string is declared literally, it is treated as a single string that includes the delimiter.

